winewayland: Office surfaces, popups and foreign toplevels.

Combined because the changes are stacked on the same functions and each
Soda userpatch must apply on its own to the pinned Valve Wine commit:
- keep a toplevel for windows with client surfaces;
- stack client surfaces in window z-order, children get no input region;
- owned tool popups (menus, flyouts) stay subsurfaces of their owner;
- popups go above all client surfaces of their toplevel;
- restack outside the win_data lock and query window geometry before
  taking it on the present path (win32u takes user_mutex before
  win_data_mutex, the old order deadlocked Outlook and OneNote);
- xdg-foreign v2 and xdg-activation v1 for embedded foreign toplevels.

